[38;2;124;124;124m2. Any two non-atomic standard probability spaces are isomorphic (mod null sets)[0m[38;2;124;124;124mto the unit interval with Lebesgue measure.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the key theorem: **The isomorphism theorem for measure spaces** [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(sometimes attributed to von Neumann, or the "standard probability space" [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtheorem). It states that any two non-atomic standard probability spaces are [0m
