[38;2;124;124;124mThe Gaussian measure on ℝ is a non-atomic probability measure, and (ℝ, B(ℝ), μ) [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis a standard probability space (since ℝ with Borel σ-algebra and a probability [0m[38;2;124;124;124mmeasure is a standard measure space).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe unit interval [0,1] with Lebesgue measure is also a non-atomic standard [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mprobability space.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore, there exists a measure-preserving isomorphism (mod null sets) φ: ℝ → [0m[38;2;124;124;124m[0,1] (between the Gaussian measure space and Lebesgue measure space).[0m

