[38;2;124;124;124m**Approach 1: Via isomorphism theorem**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe most elegant approach uses the isomorphism theorem for non-atomic standard [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mprobability spaces.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Theorem (Isomorphism of non-atomic standard probability spaces):** If (X, A, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mμ) and (Y, B, ν) are two standard probability spaces with non-atomic probability[0m[38;2;124;124;124mmeasures, then there exists a measure-preserving isomorphism between them [0m
